Task: Update the symptom areas list based on the reflection. Focus on what the triage
scan missed or should have covered.

Each item is a broad symptom area with a brief description of what to look for. Examples:
- Service-to-pod port mapping: compare every Service's targetPort against its pods' containerPort.
- Pod health: pods not in Running/Completed state.
- ConfigMap overrides: ConfigMaps that inject scripts or override entrypoints.

When to add:
- The reflection shows the triage missed a resource type or relationship that turned out
  to matter.

When to remove or refine:
- An area consistently produces benign noise that distracts the agent.
- Two items say essentially the same thing — merge them.

Rules:
- Keep the list short and high-signal. Only add items that would have changed the outcome.
  Prefer generalizing an existing item over adding a near-duplicate.
- Maximum 15 symptom areas.
- Each item must be generic (no app-specific names or values).
- Preserve items that were not implicated — do not remove working guidance.
- Output only the symptom area list (one `- ` bullet per item), no preamble or commentary.
